    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp161259520">[leum]</headword>
      <description>Leum a’ bhradain – the salmon jump, which is horizontal. Men try it but always fail.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp161261032">[traoit]</headword>
      <description>Chan eil traoit. – Not a rag. ‘Stic’ has the same meaning.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp161262544">donnalaich</headword>
      <description>wailing.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp161264056">[balg]</headword>
      <description>A’ deanamh balg ri gréin – basking in the sunshine.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp161265640">glut-lìonadh</headword>
      <description>packing the wall with earth.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp161267152">baoghal</headword>
      <description>harm, used also to mean fart.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp161268664">daorman</headword>
      <description>a little contemptible fellow.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp161270176">easbuch</headword>
